---
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About Me | Mark McManus"
	description="My background in games QA and making games at Ki10."
>
	<div class="stack gap-20">
		<main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="wrapper about">
			<Hero
				title="A bit about me"
				tagline="I’m Mark. I test games for a living, and make them at Ki10 with my friend Scott."
			>
				<img
					width="1553"
					height="873"
					src="/assets/Website about me image.JPG"
					alt="Mark McManus"
				/>
			</Hero>
			<section class="about-section">
				<h2 class="section-title">How I got here</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<p>
						I started in QA on the LEGO games. Since then I’ve worked across console, PC and mobile,
						including roles at T.T. Games, Supermassive Games, Creative Assembly and Unity. That’s
						meant testing quite a mix, from Man of Medan and Alex Kidd to Fall Guys on mobile.
					</p>
					<p>
						I’m now an <strong>Embedded QA Specialist I – Tools at Cloud Imperium Games</strong>.
						I’m the sole QA in the Tools team, testing the applications and pipelines people use to
						build Star Citizen and Squadron 42.
					</p>
					<p>
						In 2024, Scott and I started Ki10 Games. I handle design, programming and QA. We
						released Skill Check in 2026, a daily trivia game you can play on Android or in your
						browser. I’m currently working on Boop n Burn, our sixteen-player party brawler, as well
						as rebuilding KIT in Godot.
					</p>
					<p>
						Making my own games has given me plenty more to learn, especially about keeping a
						project small enough to finish. There’s more about that on the project pages.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>
			<section class="about-section">
				<h2 class="section-title">What I work with</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<p>
						Most of my QA work involves planning tests, finding and reproducing bugs, checking fixes
						and helping the team understand what needs attention. I’ve also led QA teams, mentored
						newer testers and worked on platform compliance.
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li>
							<strong>Testing:</strong> Gameplay, usability, performance, regression, tools and platform
							compliance.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Tracking and planning:</strong> Jira, DevTrack, TestRail, Redmine, QTest and Excel.
						</li>
						<li><strong>Engines:</strong> Godot, Unity, Unreal Engine 4/5 and CryEngine.</li>
						<li><strong>Programming:</strong> GDScript, C# and networked multiplayer.</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Platforms:</strong> PC, PlayStation, Xbox, Nintendo, iOS, Android and cloud gaming.
						</li>
					</ul>
					<p>My CV has the full work history.</p>
					<a href="/mark-mcmanus-cv.pdf" class="button" download>Download CV</a>
				</div>
			</section>
			<section class="about-section">
				<h2 class="section-title">Away from work</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<p>
						There’s still a fair bit of gaming, as you might expect. I also like a board game with
						friends, and I’m a lifelong Manchester United supporter.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
		<ContactCTA />
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
	.about {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 3.5rem;
	}

	img {
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
	}

	.about-section {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		color: var(--gray-200);
	}

	.section-title {
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}

	.content {
		/* No grid styles needed here by default */
	}

	.content > :global(* + *) {
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}

	.content ul {
		list-style: disc;
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
	}

	.content ul li {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	.content :global(a) {
		text-decoration: 1px solid underline transparent;
		text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition);
	}

	.content :global(a:hover),
	.content :global(a:focus) {
		text-decoration-color: currentColor;
	}

	.button {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
		background-color: var(--accent-regular);
		color: var(--accent-text-over);
		border-radius: 999px;
		text-decoration: none;
		font-weight: 500;
		transition: background-color 0.2s ease-in-out;
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}
	.button:hover {
		background-color: #922b23;
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	@media (min-width: 50em) {
		.about {
			gap: 5rem;
		}

		.about-section {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 3fr; /* Title column and Content column */
			gap: 2rem;
			font-size: var(--text-lg);
		}

		.section-title {
			grid-column: 1 / 2; /* Title takes the first column */
			text-align: right;
		}

		.content {
			grid-column: 2 / 3; /* Content takes the second column */
		}
	}
</style>
